// # oodar — Gen 1 Host Substrate (v1.0.1)
//
// Logline: The canonical home of the openOODA Gen 1 host substrate. Compiled openOODA binaries link against the oo_* symbols exported from the 6 per-domain subdirs; the build entry point is `gcc oodar.c`.
//
// Setup: Pure structural file. The 6 per-domain tactical subdirs mirror std's vocabulary (core, sec, fs, net, hw, app). Each tactical subdir has its own ANCHOR.oo. Some tactical subdirs have nested sub-subdirs (e.g., core/str/, sec/cap/, app/actor/) that also have their own ANCHOR.oo, mirroring std's per-domain organization. The umbrella oodar.c is the single-TU build entry — it #include's the 46 .c files in dependency order. The public API is oodar.h (the shared type defs in types.h) at the root.
//
// Beats (read in this order):
//   1. types.h          — shared type defs (OoStr, OoIList, OoRes*, OoLL*, OoControlBlock, OoWeakRef, ...).
//   2. oodar.h          — the public API surface.
//   3. oodar.c          — the umbrella TU (the canonical single-TU build entry).
//   4. core/            — mirrors std/core. Universal primitives: str, list, mem, math, meta.
//   5. sec/             — mirrors std/sec. Security primitives: cap (14 tokens), landlock (Pillar 9), crypto, pqc (PQC-by-default).
//   6. fs/              — mirrors std/fs. Filesystem + host OS: os (syscalls, DNS loopback, rlimit), io (print).
//   7. net/             — mirrors std/net. Network primitives: fetch, tls.
//   8. hw/              — mirrors std/hw. Hardware: gpu (HIP/ROCm, no CPU fallback).
//   9. app/             — mirrors std/app. Application bridges: actor (OTP-style concurrency), xlang (FFI), hitl (TTY), telemetry (metrics + event bus).
//  10. qa/, scripts/, docs/, examples/ — scaffolding (unchanged from v1.0.0).
//
// Naming convention:
//   - Files: <tactical>/<sub>.c  (no file prefix; one concept per file)
//   - Headers: oodar.h + types.h at root, per-subdir <thing>.h
//   - Symbols: oo_* (the openOODA namespace; language-agnostic, project-namespaced)
//   - Tactical subdirs each have an ANCHOR.oo
//   - Sub-subdirs (e.g., core/str/, sec/cap/, app/actor/) each have an ANCHOR.oo
//
// Build:
//   gcc oodar.c                           (the canonical single-TU build)
//   gcc -c <tactical>/<sub>/<file>.c      (per-file compile, link all .o)
//
// Versioning:
//   v1.0.1 is a Thrust (MINOR) bump from v1.0.0. Internal reorg only — no
//   public symbol changes, no API changes, no consumer changes.
//   See CHANGES.md for the v1.0.0 → v1.0.1 migration notes.
//   Per RULES.oot §1.24 + RFC-0006, every push to main triggers an
//   auto-release via the governance workflow.
//
// residual: dudect_c_native.c (sec/pqc/) and oo_hip_so_smoke.c (hw/gpu/) move to qa/ in a follow-up.
// residual: cap-gate the weak-ref mutators (core/mem/weak.c) — Floor break, planned for v2.0.0.
//
// ──▓▓ oodar ANCHOR ──▓▓──
// :: api_surface = 53 :: VERSION = 1.0.1 :: Pillar 5 + Pillar 7 + Pillar 9 ::
